    <title>Assignment 3 - AI Agent Deployment and Integration</title>
    <link href="/2026/05/08/assignment3.md/"/>
    <url>/2026/05/08/assignment3.md/</url>
    
    <content type="html"><![CDATA[<h1 id="Assignment-3-AI-Agent-Deployment-and-Integration"><a href="#Assignment-3-AI-Agent-Deployment-and-Integration" class="headerlink" title="Assignment 3 - AI Agent Deployment and Integration"></a>Assignment 3 - AI Agent Deployment and Integration</h1><h2 id="Student-Information"><a href="#Student-Information" class="headerlink" title="Student Information"></a>Student Information</h2><ul><li>Name: 齐永鹏</li><li>Student ID: ZY2557206</li></ul><hr><h1 id="1-Objective"><a href="#1-Objective" class="headerlink" title="1. Objective"></a>1. Objective</h1><p>The purpose of this assignment is to:</p><ul><li>Deploy and use online AI models</li><li>Deploy local large language models with Ollama</li><li>Integrate AI into the development environment</li><li>Compare online and local AI workflows</li></ul><hr><h1 id="2-Online-AI-Agent"><a href="#2-Online-AI-Agent" class="headerlink" title="2. Online AI Agent"></a>2. Online AI Agent</h1><h2 id="2-1-API-Configuration"><a href="#2-1-API-Configuration" class="headerlink" title="2.1 API Configuration"></a>2.1 API Configuration</h2><p>In this assignment, I used Dify and DeepSeek/OpenAI API to build a simple AI agent.</p><p>The AI agent can answer programming-related questions through API requests.</p><h3 id="Python-Script"><a href="#Python-Script" class="headerlink" title="Python Script"></a>Python Script</h3><figure class="highlight python"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br><span class="line">4</span><br><span class="line">5</span><br><span class="line">6</span><br><span class="line">7</span><br><span class="line">8</span><br><span class="line">9</span><br><span class="line">10</span><br><span class="line">11</span><br><span class="line">12</span><br><span class="line">13</span><br><span class="line">14</span><br><span class="line">15</span><br><span class="line">16</span><br><span class="line">17</span><br><span class="line">18</span><br><span class="line">19</span><br><span class="line">20</span><br><span class="line">21</span><br><span class="line">22</span><br><span class="line">23</span><br><span class="line">24</span><br><span class="line">25</span><br><span class="line">26</span><br><span class="line">27</span><br><span class="line">28</span><br><span class="line">29</span><br><span class="line">30</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs python"><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> requests<br><br>url = <span class="hljs-string">&quot;https://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/api/v1/services/aigc/text-generation/generation&quot;</span><br><br>headers = &#123;<br>    <span class="hljs-string">&quot;Authorization&quot;</span>: <span class="hljs-string">&quot;Bearer sk-ffda8b7341034732981a66e30e0cab8a&quot;</span>,<br>    <span class="hljs-string">&quot;Content-Type&quot;</span>: <span class="hljs-string">&quot;application/json&quot;</span><br>&#125;<br><br>data = &#123;<br>    <span class="hljs-string">&quot;model&quot;</span>: <span class="hljs-string">&quot;qwen-turbo&quot;</span>,<br>    <span class="hljs-string">&quot;input&quot;</span>: &#123;<br>        <span class="hljs-string">&quot;messages&quot;</span>: [<br>            &#123;<br>                <span class="hljs-string">&quot;role&quot;</span>: <span class="hljs-string">&quot;user&quot;</span>,<br>                <span class="hljs-string">&quot;content&quot;</span>: <span class="hljs-string">&quot;Explain matrix multiplication&quot;</span><br>            &#125;<br>        ]<br>    &#125;,<br>    <span class="hljs-string">&quot;parameters&quot;</span>: &#123;<br>        <span class="hljs-string">&quot;result_format&quot;</span>: <span class="hljs-string">&quot;message&quot;</span><br>    &#125;<br>&#125;<br><br>response = requests.post(url, headers=headers, json=data)<br><br>result = response.json()<br><br><span class="hljs-built_in">print</span>(<span class="hljs-string">&quot;AI Response:&quot;</span>)<br><span class="hljs-built_in">print</span>(result[<span class="hljs-string">&quot;output&quot;</span>][<span class="hljs-string">&quot;choices&quot;</span>][<span class="hljs-number">0</span>][<span class="hljs-string">&quot;message&quot;</span>][<span class="hljs-string">&quot;content&quot;</span>])<br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><hr><h2 id="2-2-Running-Command"><a href="#2-2-Running-Command" class="headerlink" title="2.2 Running Command"></a>2.2 Running Command</h2><figure class="highlight bash"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs bash">python agent.py<br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><hr><h2 id="2-3-Screenshot"><a href="#2-3-Screenshot" class="headerlink" title="2.3 Screenshot"></a>2.3 Screenshot</h2><h3 id="Dify-API-Configuration"><a href="#Dify-API-Configuration" class="headerlink" title="Dify API Configuration"></a>Dify API Configuration</h3><p><img src="/Assignment3/screenshots/dify_api.png" alt="Dify"></p><hr><h1 id="3-Local-Model-Deployment"><a href="#3-Local-Model-Deployment" class="headerlink" title="3. Local Model Deployment"></a>3. Local Model Deployment</h1><h2 id="3-1-Install-Ollama"><a href="#3-1-Install-Ollama" class="headerlink" title="3.1 Install Ollama"></a>3.1 Install Ollama</h2><p>I installed Ollama on Windows to deploy a local large language model.</p><h3 id="Screenshot"><a href="#Screenshot" class="headerlink" title="Screenshot"></a>Screenshot</h3><p><img src="/Assignment3/screenshots/ollama_install.png" alt="Ollama Install"></p><hr><h2 id="3-2-Pull-Local-Model"><a href="#3-2-Pull-Local-Model" class="headerlink" title="3.2 Pull Local Model"></a>3.2 Pull Local Model</h2><p>I downloaded the Qwen2 7B model using the following command:</p><figure class="highlight bash"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs bash">ollama pull qwen2:7b<br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><h3 id="Screenshot-1"><a href="#Screenshot-1" class="headerlink" title="Screenshot"></a>Screenshot</h3><p><img src="/Assignment3/screenshots/ollama_pull.png" alt="Pull Model"></p><hr><h2 id="3-3-Run-Local-Model"><a href="#3-3-Run-Local-Model" class="headerlink" title="3.3 Run Local Model"></a>3.3 Run Local Model</h2><p>After downloading the model, I used the following command to interact with it:</p><figure class="highlight bash"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs bash">ollama run qwen2:7b<br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>The model successfully generated C language bubble sort code and explanations.</p><h3 id="Screenshot-2"><a href="#Screenshot-2" class="headerlink" title="Screenshot"></a>Screenshot</h3><p><img src="/Assignment3/screenshots/ollama_run.png" alt="Run Model"></p><hr><h1 id="4-IDE-Integration"><a href="#4-IDE-Integration" class="headerlink" title="4. IDE Integration"></a>4. IDE Integration</h1><h2 id="4-1-VSCode-AI-Integration"><a href="#4-1-VSCode-AI-Integration" class="headerlink" title="4.1 VSCode AI Integration"></a>4.1 VSCode AI Integration</h2><p>I integrated AI tools into VSCode using the Continue extension.</p><p>The AI assistant can:</p><ul><li>Explain code</li><li>Generate functions</li><li>Refactor code</li><li>Help debug programs</li></ul><h3 id="Screenshot-3"><a href="#Screenshot-3" class="headerlink" title="Screenshot"></a>Screenshot</h3><p><img src="/Assignment3/screenshots/vscode_ai.png" alt="VSCode AI"></p><hr><h1 id="5-Reflection"><a href="#5-Reflection" class="headerlink" title="5. Reflection"></a>5. Reflection</h1><h2 id="Online-Model"><a href="#Online-Model" class="headerlink" title="Online Model"></a>Online Model</h2><p>Advantages:</p><ul><li>Faster response</li><li>Stronger reasoning ability</li><li>Easier to use</li></ul><p>Disadvantages:</p><ul><li>Requires Internet connection</li><li>API usage may cost money</li></ul><hr><h2 id="Local-Model"><a href="#Local-Model" class="headerlink" title="Local Model"></a>Local Model</h2><p>Advantages:</p><ul><li>Works offline</li><li>Better privacy</li><li>No API cost</li></ul><p>Disadvantages:</p><ul><li>Requires large storage space</li><li>Slower than online models</li><li>High hardware requirements</li></ul><hr><h1 id="6-Challenges-and-Solutions"><a href="#6-Challenges-and-Solutions" class="headerlink" title="6. Challenges and Solutions"></a>6. Challenges and Solutions</h1><div class="table-container"><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Solution</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>requests module missing</td><td>Installed using pip install requests</td></tr><tr><td>Python path issue</td><td>Used full Python path</td></tr><tr><td>Ollama model download slow</td><td>Waited for model pull to complete</td></tr></tbody></table></div><hr><h1 id="7-Conclusion"><a href="#7-Conclusion" class="headerlink" title="7. Conclusion"></a>7. Conclusion</h1><p>Through this assignment, I learned:</p><ul><li>How to deploy online AI agents</li><li>How to deploy local LLMs using Ollama</li><li>How to integrate AI into VSCode</li><li>The differences between online and local models</li></ul><p>This assignment improved my understanding of AI-assisted development workflows.</p>]]></content>
    
    
