    <title>Assignment 2 - Static Personal Blog Website</title>
    <link href="/2026/04/10/assignment2.md/"/>
    <url>/2026/04/10/assignment2.md/</url>
    
    <content type="html"><![CDATA[<hr><h1 id="Assignment-2-Report-–-Static-Personal-Blog-Website"><a href="#Assignment-2-Report-–-Static-Personal-Blog-Website" class="headerlink" title="Assignment 2 Report – Static Personal Blog Website"></a>Assignment 2 Report – Static Personal Blog Website</h1><h2 id="1-Introduction"><a href="#1-Introduction" class="headerlink" title="1. Introduction"></a>1. Introduction</h2><p>This project aims to build a static personal blog website using Hexo and deploy it online through GitHub Pages. The purpose of this assignment is to practice command line tools, Git version control, and static website deployment.</p><p>Through this project, a functional blog system was created where users can browse posts and download files related to the assignments.</p><p>The website is publicly accessible at:</p><p><a href="https://Qiyongpeng.github.io">https://Qiyongpeng.github.io</a></p><hr><h2 id="2-Website-Setup"><a href="#2-Website-Setup" class="headerlink" title="2. Website Setup"></a>2. Website Setup</h2><p>The blog was created using the Hexo static site generator. The following steps were taken to set up the website.</p><h3 id="Step-1-–-Install-Node-js"><a href="#Step-1-–-Install-Node-js" class="headerlink" title="Step 1 – Install Node.js"></a>Step 1 – Install Node.js</h3><p>Node.js is required for running Hexo. It was installed from the official Node.js website.</p><h3 id="Step-2-–-Install-Hexo"><a href="#Step-2-–-Install-Hexo" class="headerlink" title="Step 2 – Install Hexo"></a>Step 2 – Install Hexo</h3><p>Hexo CLI was installed globally using npm:</p><figure class="highlight avrasm"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs avrasm">npm install -g hexo-<span class="hljs-keyword">cli</span><br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><h3 id="Step-3-–-Initialize-the-Blog-Project"><a href="#Step-3-–-Initialize-the-Blog-Project" class="headerlink" title="Step 3 – Initialize the Blog Project"></a>Step 3 – Initialize the Blog Project</h3><p>A new Hexo project was created using the following command:</p><figure class="highlight mipsasm"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs mipsasm">hexo init <span class="hljs-keyword">blog</span><br><span class="hljs-keyword"></span>cd <span class="hljs-keyword">blog</span><br><span class="hljs-keyword"></span>npm <span class="hljs-keyword">install</span><br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>This command generated the basic blog structure including configuration files, themes, and directories for posts.</p><h3 id="Step-4-–-Configure-Theme"><a href="#Step-4-–-Configure-Theme" class="headerlink" title="Step 4 – Configure Theme"></a>Step 4 – Configure Theme</h3><p>The blog uses the Fluid theme to improve the visual design and layout. The theme configuration was modified in the Hexo configuration files.</p><h3 id="Step-5-–-Create-Blog-Posts"><a href="#Step-5-–-Create-Blog-Posts" class="headerlink" title="Step 5 – Create Blog Posts"></a>Step 5 – Create Blog Posts</h3><p>Two posts were created for this assignment:</p><ul><li>Assignment1 report</li><li>Assignment2 report</li></ul><p>The posts were written in Markdown format and stored in the <code>_posts</code> directory.</p><hr><h2 id="3-Git-Version-Control"><a href="#3-Git-Version-Control" class="headerlink" title="3. Git Version Control"></a>3. Git Version Control</h2><p>Git was used to manage the development process of the website. All changes were tracked using commits.</p><p>Typical commits in the project include:</p><ul><li>Initialize blog project with Hexo</li><li>Update blog configuration</li><li>Adjust theme settings</li><li>Add Assignment1 report</li><li>Add downloadable files</li><li>Update Assignment2 documentation</li></ul><p>Using Git allows the development process to be documented and provides version control for the project.</p><hr><h2 id="4-Integration-of-Assignment1"><a href="#4-Integration-of-Assignment1" class="headerlink" title="4. Integration of Assignment1"></a>4. Integration of Assignment1</h2><p>The Assignment1 report was integrated into the website as a blog post.</p><p>Users can access the Assignment1 content directly from the website and download the related files.</p><p>The following files are available for download:</p><ul><li>Markdown version of Assignment1</li><li>PDF version of Assignment1</li></ul><p>These files are stored in the <code>source/files</code> directory and linked within the blog post so that visitors can download them easily.</p><hr><h2 id="5-Website-Deployment"><a href="#5-Website-Deployment" class="headerlink" title="5. Website Deployment"></a>5. Website Deployment</h2><p>The website was deployed using GitHub Pages. This service allows static websites to be hosted directly from a GitHub repository.</p><p>The deployment process involved the following steps:</p><ol><li>Create a repository named <code>Qiyongpeng.github.io</code></li><li>Install the Hexo Git deployer plugin</li><li>Configure deployment settings in <code>_config.yml</code></li><li>Generate static files</li><li>Deploy the website using Git</li></ol><p>Deployment commands:</p><figure class="highlight css"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs css">hexo clean<br>hexo <span class="hljs-selector-tag">g</span><br>hexo d<br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>After deployment, the website became accessible through the public URL.</p><hr><h2 id="6-Conclusion"><a href="#6-Conclusion" class="headerlink" title="6. Conclusion"></a>6. Conclusion</h2><p>This assignment demonstrates how to build a static website using Hexo and manage the project using Git version control. The blog successfully integrates Assignment1 content and provides downloadable resources.</p><p>Through this project, practical experience was gained in:</p><ul><li>Command line operations</li><li>Static website generation</li><li>Git version control</li><li>Website deployment using GitHub Pages</li></ul><hr><h2 id="7-Future-Improvements"><a href="#7-Future-Improvements" class="headerlink" title="7. Future Improvements"></a>7. Future Improvements</h2><p>Although the blog is functional, several improvements could be made in the future, such as:</p><ul><li>Adding a comment system</li><li>Improving the website design and UI</li><li>Adding more blog posts and categories</li><li>Integrating search and analytics features</li></ul><p>These improvements would make the website more interactive and user-friendly.</p>]]></content>
    
    
