    <title>README</title>
    <link href="/2026/04/09/README/"/>
    <url>/2026/04/09/README/</url>
    
    <content type="html"><![CDATA[<h1 id="README"><a href="#README" class="headerlink" title="README"></a>README</h1><h1 id="Software-Technology-Course-Blog"><a href="#Software-Technology-Course-Blog" class="headerlink" title="Software Technology Course Blog"></a>Software Technology Course Blog</h1><p>This repository contains a static personal blog website created for the course <strong>Fundamentals of Software Technology</strong>.</p><p>The website is built using the Hexo static site generator and deployed through GitHub Pages. It integrates the course assignments and demonstrates the process of building, managing, and publishing a static website using command line tools and Git version control.</p><hr><h2 id="Website"><a href="#Website" class="headerlink" title="Website"></a>Website</h2><p>The blog is publicly accessible at:</p><p><a href="https://Qiyongpeng.github.io">https://Qiyongpeng.github.io</a></p><p>Visitors can browse blog posts and download assignment-related documents from the website.</p><hr><h2 id="Technologies-Used"><a href="#Technologies-Used" class="headerlink" title="Technologies Used"></a>Technologies Used</h2><p>The following tools and technologies were used in this project:</p><ul><li><strong>Node.js</strong> – Runtime environment required for Hexo</li><li><strong>Hexo</strong> – Static site generator used to build the blog</li><li><strong>Git</strong> – Version control system used to track project changes</li><li><strong>GitHub</strong> – Repository hosting and collaboration platform</li><li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong> – Website hosting service for static websites</li><li><strong>Fluid Theme</strong> – Hexo theme used to design the blog interface</li></ul><hr><h2 id="Project-Structure"><a href="#Project-Structure" class="headerlink" title="Project Structure"></a>Project Structure</h2><figure class="highlight stylus"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br><span class="line">4</span><br><span class="line">5</span><br><span class="line">6</span><br><span class="line">7</span><br><span class="line">8</span><br><span class="line">9</span><br><span class="line">10</span><br><span class="line">11</span><br><span class="line">12</span><br><span class="line">13</span><br><span class="line">14</span><br><span class="line">15</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs stylus">blog<br>│<br>├─ <span class="hljs-selector-tag">source</span><br>│   ├─ _posts<br>│   │   ├─ assignment1<span class="hljs-selector-class">.md</span><br>│   │   └─ assignment2<span class="hljs-selector-class">.md</span><br>│   │<br>│   └─ files<br>│       ├─ assignment1<span class="hljs-selector-class">.md</span><br>│       └─ assignment1<span class="hljs-selector-class">.pdf</span><br>│<br>├─ themes<br>├─ public<br>├─ _config<span class="hljs-selector-class">.yml</span><br>└─ package.json<br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><ul><li><code>_posts</code> contains the blog articles.</li><li><code>files</code> stores downloadable assignment files.</li><li><code>public</code> contains the generated static website files.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="Assignments-Included"><a href="#Assignments-Included" class="headerlink" title="Assignments Included"></a>Assignments Included</h2><h3 id="Assignment-1-–-Command-Line-amp-Documentation"><a href="#Assignment-1-–-Command-Line-amp-Documentation" class="headerlink" title="Assignment 1 – Command Line &amp; Documentation"></a>Assignment 1 – Command Line &amp; Documentation</h3><p>The Assignment1 report is included as a blog post and provides downloadable files in both Markdown and PDF formats.</p><h3 id="Assignment-2-–-Static-Personal-Blog-Website"><a href="#Assignment-2-–-Static-Personal-Blog-Website" class="headerlink" title="Assignment 2 – Static Personal Blog Website"></a>Assignment 2 – Static Personal Blog Website</h3><p>Assignment2 explains the process of:</p><ul><li>Setting up the Hexo blog</li><li>Managing the project using Git</li><li>Integrating Assignment1 into the website</li><li>Deploying the website using GitHub Pages</li></ul><hr><h2 id="Deployment-Process"><a href="#Deployment-Process" class="headerlink" title="Deployment Process"></a>Deployment Process</h2><p>The website is generated and deployed using the following Hexo commands:</p><figure class="highlight css"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs css">hexo clean<br>hexo <span class="hljs-selector-tag">g</span><br>hexo d<br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>These commands generate static files and deploy them to the GitHub Pages repository.</p><hr><h2 id="Author"><a href="#Author" class="headerlink" title="Author"></a>Author</h2><p>Qi Yongpeng</p><p>Course: Fundamentals of Software Technology</p>]]></content>
    
    
